    # 972 조합 증서 쪽 (+ 봉랍 확인)
    "You can buy and sell certificates of the town's six unions (Farmers' · Fishers' · Smiths' · Grocers' · Land Union · Survey Corps Fund).\n\n"
    "· Talk to the banker and choose [Exchange] to buy certificates at today's price and sell them back. Buying and selling each carry a fee (2% by default).\n"
    "· Prices change once a day. When the server's money flow on that union's side (selling crops, fish, ores and dishes, buying from the smithy and enhancing, land, raids, the Abyss and bounties) runs above usual, the price rises; below usual, it falls. A day moves at most ±10%.\n"
    "· When the server first passes a big moment of the story, the news moves the prices.\n"
    "· Market events happen too: now and then when the day turns (30% by default) a bumper crop, a storm warning, a new ore vein, a festival or a land rush moves one union by 3–8%, and some of it comes back the next day. After a long thunderstorm a storm warning may follow, and on Saturdays the market may open.\n"
    "· Dividends are set every week. Show the banker certificates you have held since last week to collect them; the certificate gets a stamp. Dividends come only from the fund the fees fill.\n"
    "· Certificates can be handed over or put in a player shop, and are kept when you fall. A certificate that is not in the ledger (a copy) is not accepted.\n"
    "· The Union Price Board (block) or /rtshop stocks shows the last 14 days of prices and the news. Right-clicking a certificate works too.\n"
    "· At the counter, [Check] next to a certificate has the exchange check its seal for a small fee (1% of its face value, at least 100 G). A certificate bought from another player is worth checking.",
    # 973
